on in the building So we've been working with Ed surface and PCS to get that written out What I've given you is the latest version of that So what I'm asking for is for you guys to approve the quote and the agreement","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3813-139","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3813,"timestampLabel":"1:03:33","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- pending satisfactory language, which I expect to have soon, so that they can get this work done during the summer and hopefully have it ready before school year starts and that all of this is completed. So asking for approve that pending satisfactory language, the quote in the corresponding agreement. I'll second. Second, any discussion? Just curiosity, how big a space are we talking about?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3839-140","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3839,"timestampLabel":"1:03:59","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- I don't recall the total square footage off the top of my head, but if you know where the teachers lounge access area is to the junior high, you walk in and you look to the left. So kind of where that little hallway is, that wall would go along where that hallway is. So it's still have that access hallway to get into the media center in that place, but it would wall that off. And then there'd be a door cut on the outside wall. That would be a direct access from the hallway into that room. Yeah, it's not, it's not, no, no, it's,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3869-141","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3869,"timestampLabel":"1:04:29","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And it's a much better utilization of that space than what it's being used for now. It's gonna be able to serve students, which is obviously a great thing. It'd be done this summer. So hopefully pending approval from you all, I'll be getting out that confirmation to them tomorrow so that they can get it scheduled because if not, if we had to wait till July, there's just no way that we would have the opportunity to get this work done. So we're really gonna be pushing on them to get this completed and finished before next school year starts.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3900-142","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3900,"timestampLabel":"1:05:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Mr. Siegel, does this make sense? This is what you guys want, right? Yeah, we're really limited in the office space and giving up an office to utilize it as high as this right now is a short-term fix on the long-term and something we really need. And for the number of teachers that utilize that space, we've got another space of mind that we can use. Is this like a 10 by 10 or a 20 by 20? I would say it's a whole pack.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3929-143","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3929,"timestampLabel":"1:05:29","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- 16 by 16, maybe 16 by 20, something like that. It's not a full classroom, but it's big enough to do. It would have to be for an extra suspension. Yeah, and it's, I mean, right now we're utilizing a space where we can only fit three students, four students maybe, or they're sitting on top of each other. Which, at the end of the break, they don't need to be sitting on top of each other anyway. But to go is not to have it, period.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3955-144","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3955,"timestampLabel":"1:05:55","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- We just need us we just need us we just need a space Did we have a motion, yes, was it contingent on the review by legal? Okay","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-3982-145","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":3982,"timestampLabel":"1:06:22","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Okay, there's nothing else all those in favor say aye aye opposed motion carries Thank you. And now we look at the renewal of the IU health athletic trainer agreement mr. Wang","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4011-146","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4011,"timestampLabel":"1:06:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Yeah, so last year was the first year that we had this agreement in place. This is a continuation of that agreement, obviously, but this is for a multi-year agreement. So not a whole lot of changes to the structure of the agreement. The initial price for this year is the exact same as what it was last year, but what they did was put a 3% escalator in it for each year just for it to keep up with cost of living and to keep that person's salary and benefits moving.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4038-147","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4038,"timestampLabel":"1:07:18","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Everything else is pretty close to the same. They made some slight tweaks to the marketing pieces that they would like in exchange for the sharing of costs for an athletic trainer. Looked into those some more. I don't think that it's gonna pose an issue to the school. It's not really any different than what we're doing now. And so this is just a partnership that we have with IU where they're helping to share in the cost of what it is to provide an athletic trainer to our teams.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4064-148","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4064,"timestampLabel":"1:07:44","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- At this point, we're very happy with where we're at with this, so I'm recommending your approval of this renewal. I'll move approval. I second. The cost of it? $43,000, and then next year it will go up by 3% each year thereafter. Any further? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Now permission to create the position of a certified","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-408-15","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":408,"timestampLabel":"6:48","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And he proceeds to tell me that he has this other business that he started on his own. It has to do with shoes. And I mean, it's just remarkable how he is able to use the technology to buy the shoes at a low price. And then he sells them. And that's his student-run business on his own. And then I just got to tell this because it's just so exciting.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4094-149","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4094,"timestampLabel":"1:08:14","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- occupational therapy assistant. Yes, so in the past we have had a contract with an outside company to provide the services of a certified occupational therapist assistant. We feel like we could possibly save the corporation some money by hiring this person directly. And so in order to do that, we have to create this position.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4122-150","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4122,"timestampLabel":"1:08:42","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And so we recommend your approval of that tonight. I'll second. You can second. Any discussion? Just curiosity, what do you anticipate that the cost would be for this person? Matt, do you know that?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4142-151","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4142,"timestampLabel":"1:09:02","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- You probably set the hourly rate somewhere in the mid 20s as far as what the going rate is. We're gonna continue to kind of look at what the analysis of what the going rate is for that. If we had to work with a contracting company, the markup on that is pretty extreme. And so we think that if we're able to find the right person, this would be a much better service to the kids and to the school corporation on every side of the spectrum.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4169-152","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4169,"timestampLabel":"1:09:29","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- This could be reimbursing some through maybe some Medicaid reimbursement. Yeah, I have to double check on on that on that, but I believe so. I think there's probably a little bit different reimbursement rates as it relates to different levels of professionals on licensing, but that would be something that if we're able to reimburse will continue to do that just like we build Medicaid services for those that are eligible to to bill. So they'll get benefits too. This is going to be a part time","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4200-153","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4200,"timestampLabel":"1:10:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And Next would be the creation of a position for a speech-language pathologist assistant Yes, so The purpose of this new position would really be to support our SLP's Kara glasscock who serves EPS and Justin Ross to who serves","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4228-154","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4228,"timestampLabel":"1:10:28","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- at the Edgewood Early Childhood Center. They've been doing a fantastic job trying to keep up with the growing demands, growing caseload. And so we feel though in order to support them, it would be really beneficial for the corporation to create this","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4251-155","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4251,"timestampLabel":"1:10:51","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- a speech and language pathologist assistant position so we can help take a little bit of the caseload off of these two fine educators. Last year we had had a, the board had approved an agreement for an outside,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4267-156","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4267,"timestampLabel":"1:11:07","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- to provide that and we can get a lot more hours out of someone and a lot more service to kids for a lot cheaper costs if we're able to hire them directly rather than paying all the markup fees and get more time. So the idea is that it would be a part-time position and it would even then be a step up in some of the services and some of the help that we're able to provide our SLPs. I move approval of creation of the. I second. Any discussion?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4297-157","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4297,"timestampLabel":"1:11:37","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Now consideration of the agreement for a memorandum of understanding with the South Central Community Action Program head start. Mr. Irwin. Yeah, so you guys saw Jennifer Anderson's memo on this. This is something that as a renewal, we do it every two years. There's been no changes from the last MOU. It was reviewed by Jessica Heiser, who's a special education attorney that we use through imprint legal group.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4327-158","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4327,"timestampLabel":"1:12:07","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And again, and just make sure that there's coordination of services for the students that need them from early intervention services, part C to preschool special education services, part B, if eligible and are at headstart. I move approval. I'll second. Moved and second. Any discussion? All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Now consideration to approve the 2020","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4357-159","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4357,"timestampLabel":"1:12:37","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- 2025-2026 classified handbook. Mr. Irwin. Yeah, so I put just one pager there in front of you because there was one adjustment I needed to make. I had gotten a last minute feedback from one of our directors on a question that I felt like this was something. So if you look at the page that's there in front of you at the bottom, the second piece that's in red, it says days to be used at the discretion of department supervisors or superintendent.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-437-16","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":437,"timestampLabel":"7:17","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- 10th birthday, 10 years old, Jackson took his money that he got for his birthday and invested it in stocks. Yeah, so. I didn't think he was impressive before the launch, after the launch. That's all we talked about on the way back. Yeah. I think I need to meet with him. Wow. And remember, he was just like, I mean, he used himself to put money in.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4386-160","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4386,"timestampLabel":"1:13:06","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So we had added in the three e-learning pay days for transportation and nutrition services staff. That was to make sure that some of our employees who don't have an opportunity to make up work when we are out of school have a protection to their paycheck. What this is, is to make sure that when we have a flex day and it's not bad weather, if there's work for them to do,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4411-161","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4411,"timestampLabel":"1:13:31","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- then obviously we're gonna have them come in and do that work, whether it's training or being better at some of the surfaces that we need for them to work on. And so that's something that's just saying, hey, there is that flexibility. It's a clarification of what we're already doing. But again, one of the goals every year when we review this is to say, is there something that we need to clarify? And also, is there something that we need to change? And so this would be something that's just a clarification of how we already administer that as well. But again, the sole purpose of it's there","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4440-162","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4440,"timestampLabel":"1:14:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- to protect that, so if they're not used on flex day and say we have a really bad winter and we have to take several e-learning days, those three e-learning days that we're allowed to use asynchronously, it protects the paycheck of those employees who don't have much of an opportunity to make up work when we continue to be outside of school.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4458-163","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4458,"timestampLabel":"1:14:18","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- The other changes that were in the classified handbook, again, I put those in red that was reviewed by Christine. I put those in red just so you didn't have to read every piece of that, but it kind of points you to these are the major changes or these are the things that are changing from one year to the next. But this is something that you review multiple times a year as it relates to the handbook. So asking for your approval of that. I'll make approval. I second.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4486-164","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4486,"timestampLabel":"1:14:46","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Quick question on the preschool secretary we That was a we were moving into the school secretary category transferred over to the school secretary scale again Just because we didn't exit. Yes. Yeah, so there was no point to have it on there anymore because with the","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4503-165","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4503,"timestampLabel":"1:15:03","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- creation of the new building, doubling the size, daycare, all the things that are going on there. There's a little bit more alignment with that and there's not the other assistance there in the office. So bringing some of those things into alignment and again, just making adjustments to the handbook over time as it makes sense as things continue to evolve from school year to school year. Yeah, appreciate cleaning that up. Okay, all those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4534-166","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4534,"timestampLabel":"1:15:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Now consideration to approve the 2025 2026 before and after care handbook. Yeah, so bright bringing this to you because again with the change in the preschool again adding more opportunity for kids to have before and after care if they're in the preschool.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4554-167","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4554,"timestampLabel":"1:15:54","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And so this was something we've made several changes to it, felt like it was something that we needed to start bringing to you each year to review. The rates that are in the back end of it is something that you guys have already reviewed earlier in the year, just because we need to set those rates earlier as we are releasing information to families about that are looking into preschool or that are getting ready for kindergarten roundup or whatever that might be. So some of that stuff is some things that you've already seen before, but with some of these changes felt like it was necessary to start to bring that to you. And again,","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4584-168","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4584,"timestampLabel":"1:16:24","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- and will be under the direction of Heather Kenzik. She'll oversee the before and aftercare director. She'll still obviously work with the EPS and EIS administration to coordinate those services in those buildings, but she'll help with making sure that things are billing and all those other pieces are running the way that they should. So with that, asking for your approval on the before and aftercare handbook. Any discussion?","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4613-169","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4613,"timestampLabel":"1:16:53","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. No consideration to approve the 2025-2026 student parent handbooks. Dr. Sanders. Yes, so I was just thinking about this. The handbooks are probably one of the most valuable documents that we have because it's such an effective way to communicate with parents and provide them with valuable information","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4640-170","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4640,"timestampLabel":"1:17:20","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- on procedures and other information that they need to know as parents. And so if you look at our handbooks, they're very well done. Our principals put a lot of time and energy into that. And every year, you kind of evaluate and think back on the past school year and different things that have come up. And then the principals think, well, we could better word that. And so they make revisions to the handbook.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-467-17","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":467,"timestampLabel":"7:47","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- So much intelligence and even mr. Durham put two and two together All right, that's all for me Did you guys already vote on the consent agenda","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4670-171","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4670,"timestampLabel":"1:17:50","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- or there might be new laws that the state legislators have provided us. And so we include those changes in the handbooks. We run those all by Christine and she just loves that time of the year when she could look at all the handbooks and she's very, she does a very good job at that and I really appreciate that. So we recommend your approval.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4700-172","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4700,"timestampLabel":"1:18:20","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- student parent handbooks. I'll second. All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. I have consideration to approve power school section 504 software program contract. Mr. Erwin.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4719-173","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4719,"timestampLabel":"1:18:39","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Yeah, so this brings into alignment the state moved to power school being the provider of the new IEP platform as well. So it brings into alignment our section 504 plans in the IEP program being on the same platform, which makes it a lot easier for staff to make sure that we're administering the pieces that we need to for the students that get those services. So it was reviewed by Ferguson law. There was one change that needed to be made to it as it related to auto renewal.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4747-174","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4747,"timestampLabel":"1:19:07","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- That change has been made. So the agreement that you will be able to sign or approve at this point, Dr. Sanders will sign after pending your approval. It does have the auto renewal out of it, which is what Christine wanted to be out of it. They agreed to that change. So at this point, everything's good to go. So asking for your approval of that, please. I'll move approval. I'll second.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4771-175","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4771,"timestampLabel":"1:19:31","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- a set price contract, or is it? Yeah, so each year there's a set price. So year one, 25 to 26, is $5,822.50. Year two is $1,640.35. And then the years after, it has those in there as far as what those prices are. And then it has the subscription pieces that are in it. And it has the different layers in it as far as product services, training services. Training is $855.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4801-176","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4801,"timestampLabel":"1:20:01","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- so it lays out the different pieces that are in it. All those in favor say aye. Aye. Opposed? Motion carries. Okay, now we're to our friendly superintendent's report. You know, I just love this report tonight because so many times when I'm out and about, sometimes the public thinks that","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4830-177","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4830,"timestampLabel":"1:20:30","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- school corporations shut down during the summer.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4834-178","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4834,"timestampLabel":"1:20:34","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And I just wanted to give a report tonight to demonstrate that really our campus never sleeps. It's maybe moratorium week. It slows down a little bit. So our wonderful nutrition department is always on the move. As you know, they're providing free breakfast and lunch to students participating in summer school. We have the summer","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4860-179","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4860,"timestampLabel":"1:21:00","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- feeding program, which provides individual breakfast and lunch meals, which goes from May 28th through July 25th. And so there's different pickup points.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4873-180","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4873,"timestampLabel":"1:21:13","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- that the community can go to to get those individual lunches. And one of those would be our food truck that they could go to a location and utilize our food truck for those individual meals. This summer, we've added something, and that's the summer meal pickup. So a family can pick up a meal for a week, five breakfasts, five lunch meals, and a gallon of milk per child.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-4900-181","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":4900,"timestampLabel":"1:21:40","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And so that goes from June 4th through July 23rd. And it's a drive-through service that's behind EPS. And I think that's pretty cool that we serve 