. I'm sorry, this is gonna be difficult. I'm asking everybody to please keep Cindy Bentley's family very close to their hearts. I've known Cindy for a lot of years.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5099-189","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5099,"timestampLabel":"1:24:59","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- And it's going to be difficult. And I haven't earned our corporation. We need to make sure we're rallying around the staff that have worked with her for so many years because they're hurting. And her grandchildren are RBB students. So we need to make sure that we're rallying around them and supporting them. Thank you. Mr. Tucker.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5128-190","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-transcript","sourceLabel":"Video Transcript","sourceUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","videoUrl":"https://catstv.net/m.php?q=14701","timestampSeconds":5128,"timestampLabel":"1:25:28","speakerName":null,"speakerConfidence":"unknown","text":"- Yeah, just continued prayers for that family and for the community to wrap their arms around the Bailey family and help them through this time. And also for the family in Owen County that was affected as well. So appreciate all the information tonight and good meeting. If I can get it out, thank you, Matt, for all your work you've done for us and Jerry.","transcriptMethod":"publisher-caption","official":false,"ingestion":"auto"},{"id":"cats-14701-tx-5156-191","meetingDate":"2025-06-17","meetingTitle":"Richland Bean Blossom School Board 6/17/2025","sourceType":"video-